1. Definitions

  "Software" means the source code, shaders, binaries, documentation,
  assets, and any other material in this repository.

  "Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not primarily intended for, or
  directed toward, commercial advantage or monetary compensation. Personal
  study, hobby projects, academic research, and teaching are examples of
  Non-Commercial Use.

  "AI Training" means using the Software itself (its source code, shaders,
  documentation, or other contents of this repository), in whole or in
  part, as training data or as other input to build, train, fine-tune,
  evaluate, benchmark, or otherwise improve any machine learning model,
  large language model, code-generation system, or other artificial
  intelligence system, including by placing the Software in any dataset,
  corpus, or retrieval index intended for such purposes.

  "AI Replication" means using an AI system (for example, an LLM or
  code-generation tool) to reproduce, re-create, rewrite, port to another
  language, or otherwise generate a new project that is a copy of, or
  substantially similar to, the Software or a substantial part of it,
  where the result is presented or distributed as a separate work not
  covered by this license.

  "AI-Assisted Modification" means using an AI system as a development
  aid to read, understand, fix, or extend your own copy or fork of the
  Software, where the result remains a derivative work of the Software
  covered by this license.

  "Framework Use" means running the Software as an engine, simulator, or
  environment, including using its built-in features to train, run, or
  evaluate models (for example, reinforcement learning agents) that learn
  from the simulation, observations, or data produced while the Software
  runs, rather than from the contents of the Software itself.

